---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`How ${site.name} is maintained.`} current="about">
  <p class="kicker">About</p>
  <h1>One JSON file per day</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    {site.name} publishes short research and reception briefs for SMB operations.
    The pages do not change when a new day lands. The content file does.
  </p>

  <h2>How it is maintained</h2>
  <p>
    Grok Bot (or anyone else) adds a daily update by creating
    <code>content/updates/YYYY-MM-DD.json</code>. The filename and the
    <code>date</code> field must match. A Zod schema in
    <code>src/content.config.ts</code> validates the shape at build time. Bad
    content fails the build instead of shipping a broken page.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is no CMS, database, or login. Layout, typography, and routes stay in
    the Astro project. A new day is never a reason to edit a component.
  </p>

  <h2>What an update contains</h2>
  <ul class="about-list">
    <li>A title and a short summary (the TL;DR callout on the detail page)</li>
    <li>Optional tone, for readers who want the stance in one word</li>
    <li>Sections with a heading, bullets, and optional labeled sources</li>
    <li>A bottom line that a busy operator can act on</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to read it</h2>
  <p>
    Home shows the latest brief and a chronological archive. Each day has a
    permalink at <code>/updates/YYYY-MM-DD/</code>. An RSS feed is at
    <a href="/rss.xml">/rss.xml</a>. Sources are public coverage links, not
    invented metrics.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
